<rss version="0.92"><channel><item>
            <title>[LU-21329] rustreapi: build fails against 2.17.50-2.17.58 headers (volatile calls gated on LUSTRE_2_18)</title>
                <link>https://jira.whamcloud.com/browse/LU-21329</link>
                <project id="10000" key="LU">Lustre</project>
                    <description>&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href="https://jira.whamcloud.com/browse/LU-18842" title="lustreapi: add a volatile function that supports layouts" class="issue-link" data-issue-key="LU-18842"&gt;&lt;del&gt;LU-18842&lt;/del&gt;&lt;/a&gt; added &lt;tt&gt;llapi_file_open_volatile_param()&lt;/tt&gt; and &lt;tt&gt;llapi_layout_file_open_volatile()&lt;/tt&gt;, which first ship in 2.17.59. rustreapi's &lt;tt&gt;OpenOptions::volatile()&lt;/tt&gt; calls them under the &lt;tt&gt;LUSTRE_2_18&lt;/tt&gt; feature.  lu-version sets that feature for any installed 2.17.50 or later, so a build against 2.17.50-2.17.58 headers fails:&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;div class="preformatted panel" style="border-width: 1px;"&gt;&lt;div class="preformattedContent panelContent"&gt;
&lt;pre&gt;error[E0425]: cannot find function `llapi_file_open_volatile_param` in this scope
error[E0425]: cannot find function `llapi_layout_file_open_volatile` in this scope
&lt;/pre&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Reproduced with master's rustreapi and the 2.17.53 headers.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;The fix does what &lt;a href="https://jira.whamcloud.com/browse/LU-20663" title="rustreapi: lsp_stripe_pattern union breaks build against master lustreapi.h" class="issue-link" data-issue-key="LU-20663"&gt;LU-20663&lt;/a&gt; does for the stripe pattern union: probe the generated bindings rather than the version.  lustreapi-sys/build.rs looks for &lt;tt&gt;llapi_file_open_volatile_param&lt;/tt&gt; and passes the result to rustreapi as links metadata (&lt;tt&gt;DEP_LUSTREAPI_HAS_FILE_OPEN_VOLATILE&lt;/tt&gt;). rustreapi/build.rs turns it into the &lt;tt&gt;has_file_open_volatile&lt;/tt&gt; cfg.  A layout test checks that a stripe pattern given to &lt;tt&gt;OpenOptions&lt;/tt&gt; reaches the file through both &lt;tt&gt;open()&lt;/tt&gt; and &lt;tt&gt;volatile()&lt;/tt&gt;.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Depends on &lt;a href="https://jira.whamcloud.com/browse/LU-20663" title="rustreapi: lsp_stripe_pattern union breaks build against master lustreapi.h" class="issue-link" data-issue-key="LU-20663"&gt;LU-20663&lt;/a&gt;.  In Gerrit it is stacked on &lt;a href="https://jira.whamcloud.com/browse/LU-6142" title="Enforce Linux kernel coding style in all code" class="issue-link" data-issue-key="LU-6142"&gt;LU-6142&lt;/a&gt;, which is on &lt;a href="https://jira.whamcloud.com/browse/LU-20210" title="rustre: export nodemap_rbac_roles" class="issue-link" data-issue-key="LU-20210"&gt;LU-20210&lt;/a&gt;, &lt;a href="https://jira.whamcloud.com/browse/LU-20664" title="rustreapi: lsp_pool is set from an unterminated Rust String" class="issue-link" data-issue-key="LU-20664"&gt;LU-20664&lt;/a&gt; and &lt;a href="https://jira.whamcloud.com/browse/LU-20663" title="rustreapi: lsp_stripe_pattern union breaks build against master lustreapi.h" class="issue-link" data-issue-key="LU-20663"&gt;LU-20663&lt;/a&gt;.  &lt;a href="https://jira.whamcloud.com/browse/LU-20208" title="Allow rustreapi documentation to be generated by docs.rs" class="issue-link" data-issue-key="LU-20208"&gt;LU-20208&lt;/a&gt; (docs.rs) skips bindgen, so whichever of the two lands second must set this cfg from the docs snapshot too.&lt;/p&gt;</description>
